IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`

-- P8-gate: the helpers that every P8 module uses to call the keel's applicability function.
-- Nothing here is a provision of Articles 72 to 79 and nothing restates a date: each function only passes
-- the provision group to `Art 113 the provision group applies` (aia-timeline.l4), which is the one applicability function.
-- Every name here begins `Arts 72 to 79` (the part's own label, as there is no single Article) or `Art 78`.

§ `Articles 72 to 77 and 79 are in the group General; Article 78 is in the group of 2 August 2025`

-- A question about one AI system: the route, the placement date and the design-change fact go to the keel
-- (Art 111(2) can save a system placed on the market before Chapter III applies to it).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies to the AI system` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`

-- A question that is not about one AI system (the keel's constants stand in for the system).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

-- Article 78 only: the group `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78`.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE

GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies to the AI system` MEANS
    `Art 113 the provision group applies` `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`

§ `Seam S14: Article 2(2) cuts off a provision about a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products`

-- Article 2(2) (the keel, aia-scope.l4) says that for such a system "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply", so no provision of
-- Articles 72 to 79 applies to it. This helper asks the keel's `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products`
-- about one provision of this part (its Article number and paragraph) and answers TRUE only where the keel answers JUST FALSE; where the keel answers NOTHING
-- (the system is not of that kind, or Chapter I does not apply yet) Article 2(2) does not speak and the function that calls this helper answers on its own provision.
-- Which functions call it is fork F-S14-reach (assumed, not ruled; NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of the Article` IS A NUMBER
      `the paragraph of the Article` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 2(2) the provision applies to the high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the provision cited`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST `it applies` THEN NOT `it applies`
    WHERE
        `the provision cited` MEANS `Article reference` WITH
            number IS `the number of the Article`
            letter IS ""
            paragraph IS `the paragraph of the Article`

§ `The classification seam (S1): an AI system is high-risk if and only if its route is not Route neither`

-- PLAN.md section 4, seam S1: the route comes from Article 6 (another part); a high-risk AI system is one whose route is not `Route neither`.
GIVEN `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Arts 72 to 79 the AI system is a high-risk AI system` MEANS
    `the route to high-risk` EQUALS `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` OR `the route to high-risk` EQUALS `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III`

§ `The parties of the regulative rules of Articles 72 to 79`

-- The roles of the core cover the operators; the authorities and the Commission are parties of the rules
-- of this part, so this one type carries every party named in Articles 72 to 79. It is a type of nouns only.
DECLARE `Arts 72 to 79 party` IS ONE OF
    `Arts 72 to 79 party provider`
    `Arts 72 to 79 party deployer`
    `Arts 72 to 79 party operator`
    `Arts 72 to 79 party notified body`
    `Arts 72 to 79 party market surveillance authority`
    `Arts 72 to 79 party national competent authority`
    `Arts 72 to 79 party national public authority protecting fundamental rights`
    `Arts 72 to 79 party AI Office`
    `Arts 72 to 79 party Commission`
    `Arts 72 to 79 party Member State`
    `Arts 72 to 79 party national judicial authority`
    `Arts 72 to 79 party Court of Justice of the European Union`
    `Arts 72 to 79 party any other person involved in the application of this Regulation`
